### `kustomize.yaml`

We've enabled kustomization so that we can easily manage all of our Kubernetes resources in one place. To learn more about Kustomize, see the [Kubernetes Best Practices](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubectl/blob/master/examples/best-practices.md#using-kustomize-to-manage-your-resources).

### `application-config.yaml`

In addition to the kustomizations, we also include some additional configurations for our application here:

* `deployment`: We specify multiple replicas for each deployment, which allows us to scale out our service horizontally when needed.
* `targetPorts`: Specify the port numbers that each container exposes.
* `env`: Add environment variables to the containers, such as logging level and maximum connections.
* `secret`: Store secrets in our secret store, including tokens and passwords, and make them available to pods via volumes or environment variables.
* `ingress`: Configure ingress rules to route requests to our application based on hostnames and paths.
